  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **NFA**: back after 94 archived shows (1422 days); rare: 3 archived performances [8]\n- **NFA**: back after 94 archived shows (1422 days); rare: 3 archived performances [8]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **deadco2023-05-06.mk41v.flac24** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 13 songs; 148 min; rated 4.67/5 by 3 [1]. Said about its sound: Reviewer found the recording sounds very good, better than the description led them to expect, given the recording conditions; Reviewer calls it a fine recording given festival circumstances, and was pleasantly surprised by it; Described as a warts-and-all tape, with stout wind throughout, especially heavy until Brown Eyed Women [1][5][7]\n- **deadco2023-05-06.lineaudiocm3.oadedr100**: source not stated; 12 songs; 145 min; rated 4/5 by 1 [2]. Said about its sound: Rain and gusts cause wind noise and phasey treble; nearby chatty crowd conversation is audible throughout [2]\n- **deadco2023-05-06**: source not stated; 10 songs; 72 min [3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Reviewer describes a taping trick at the race track: skull-topped pole with mics in the eye sockets, decorated with beads and flags [6]\n- Taper's gear was soaked for hours by rain; mics went up only minutes before the band started, and wind is strong early on [1]\n- North Side Skull and Bones Gang made a special appearance during the show [2]\n- Set ran 4:30pm to 7pm on the Festival Stage; lineup included Weir, Mayer, Burbridge, Chimenti and Jay Lane [3]\n- Recording begins at 5:49pm, missing about the first 80 minutes, because the taper stayed to watch Dee Dee Bridgewater [3]\n- Reviewer says many listeners criticize this show, but the band still jammed and it was fun to hear [7]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **deadco2023-05-06.mk41v.flac24**: taped by teamikoiko; transferred by teamikoiko; source: Schoeps mk41v (ortf, 6.5 ft, @ sbd, slightly right of center) > nbob/Naiant PFA > MixPre 6 II @ 32/44.1 [1]. Also: Schoeps mk41v mics in ORTF, 6.5 feet high near the soundboard, through Naiant PFA preamps to a MixPre 6 II at 32-bit/44.1 [1]\n- **deadco2023-05-06.lineaudiocm3.oadedr100**: taped by goodcooker; transferred by goodcooker; source: Line Audio CM3 > Oade Concert Mod Tascam DR100mkII [2]\n- **deadco2023-05-06**: taped by Funk It Blog; transferred by Funk It Blog; source: Shure MV88 > iPhone 7 > Motiv Audio App > WAV [3]. Also: Recorded on a Shure MV88 mic into an iPhone 7 with Motiv app, converted to 24/48 FLAC [3]",
